From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:52:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec: bound the wait for a picture

Once a packet was in, receive waited for a picture without end. A
decoder that needs more input before its next picture, or whose
capture buffers the caller still holds, then never returned: the
caller, stopping, could not join its decoding thread (the stick's
player froze on leaving a 4K film). Wait at most
V4L2_RECEIVE_WAIT_MS and return EAGAIN, as a freed input buffer
already does; draining still waits for the end. Applies after the
DRM PRIME series.
---
 libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m_dec.c
@@ -41,6 +41,10 @@
 #include "v4l2_m2m.h"
 #include "v4l2_fmt.h"
 
+/* How long a picture is waited for once a packet is in, before the caller
+ * is let go (EAGAIN) to send more or to stop. */
+#define V4L2_RECEIVE_WAIT_MS 100
+
 static const enum AVPixelFormat v4l2_m2m_pix_fmts[] = {
     AV_PIX_FMT_DRM_PRIME,
     AV_PIX_FMT_NV12,
@@ -227,7 +231,7 @@
     }
 
 dequeue:
-    return ff_v4l2_context_dequeue_frame(capture, frame, -1);
+    return ff_v4l2_context_dequeue_frame(capture, frame, s->draining ? -1 : V4L2_RECEIVE_WAIT_MS);
 fail:
     av_packet_unref(&s->buf_pkt);
     return ret;
